  <description>
    <p>From survey points to finished grade. CivilCraft is part of the CadCraft family: eight free, open-source apps (Apache-2.0) for drafting, modeling, review and takeoff.</p>
    <p>What you can do in CivilCraft preview:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Import survey points</li>
      <li>Edit a survey point</li>
      <li>Elevation grids and LiDAR</li>
      <li>Select, copy and paste survey points</li>
      <li>Description keys and line codes</li>
      <li>Build and refine the surface</li>
      <li>Open a DWG or DXF as linework</li>
      <li>Read contours, elevations and slopes</li>
      <li>Lay out a horizontal alignment</li>
      <li>Design a vertical profile</li>
      <li>Sample lines and cross sections</li>
      <li>Plan and profile sheets</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your files stay on your computer: nothing is uploaded, and the app never contacts getcadcraft.com. Map layers from the internet are off until you turn them on in Settings; then the map tiles come from the services you choose. A grid shift file you choose to download comes from the PROJ project's server. Every feature is free, for any work, commercial work included. No account, no sign-in, no ads. Works offline.</p>
    <p>This is an early release (preview). Help is built in, and the help says plainly what is not built yet.</p>
  </description>
